# Analytics SPOCs

Every organisation with access to GOV.UK web analytics data should have a nominated Analytics Single Point of Contact (SPOC).

## SPOC responsibilities 
The primary responsibility of the SPOC is to maintain appropriate access to GOV.UK Google Analytics 4 data within their organisation.

This includes:

- raising requests to grant new users GOV.UK Google Analytics access, for example when new starters join the organisation
- raising requests to remove GOV.UK Google Analytics access from users who no longer need it, for example when users leave the organisation
- monitoring which employees at their organisation have Google Analytics access
- carrying out a review of GA4 access every 6 months and sending a list of users who no longer require access

SPOCs can use some basic reporting provided (see below) to enable them to [monitor their organisation's users' usage](/products/govuk-ga4-spocs/).

## How to become a SPOC
To request a change of SPOC, raise a request via the [Analytics Support Form](https://support.publishing.service.gov.uk/analytics_request/new) or govuk-ga4-support@digital.cabinet-office.gov.uk stating who the new SPOC will be.

The nominated SPOC will need access to Signon. Access to Signon can be arranged by your organisation's content SPOC.

## Resources for SPOCs

### Requesting or removing user access

There are two main ways to submit requests for new users or users who no longer require access.

1. **Analytics Support Form**

If you have access to GOV.UK Sign-on, you should raise a ticket using the [Analytics Support form](https://support.publishing.service.gov.uk/analytics_request/new).

2. **GOV.UK GA4 Support**

If you do not have access to Support Form, please email, **govuk-ga4-support@digital.cabinet-office.gov.uk**

Include:
- the names and email addresses of the users
- the relevant organisation or department
- whether access is being requested or removed

## Monitoring users

Use the [SPOC user report](https://lookerstudio.google.com/reporting/3efb1388-9c6f-4265-beea-caea6b5a89fb/page/3GYgD)

If you cannot access the report or have any other questions, please contact the [GOV.UK GA4 support inbox](mailto:govuk-ga4-support@digital.cabinet-office.gov.uk).
